Z||000000||Santa Cruzer||08-08-2001||06:03 PM||||so do i goto a yard find a 87 grand am and up, and just take the calipers off? is that all?<P>------------------<BR>BlOw bIg cHuNkS oF aMeRiCaN v6 YoU rIcE CrApEr'S! <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/se.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/se.html</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||08-08-2001||06:52 PM||||No, you need the rotors too. Then take a set of Fiero front hubs and have the rotors milled off down to the size where they will fit into the center of the GA rotors. Then, press out the lugs and install longer ones. I know some people skip that part, but I think it's a good idea.<P>Then remove the caliper bracket from the spindle and grind off the boss that now hits the GA rotors. Pre-assembly the hubs, rotors and calipers on the car and you will see what needs to be removed.<P>Search the internet for Fiero Grand Am and a billion sites will pop up with the details.<P>TK||||reg||1
